---
title: "G9 Frametop Together: the units, a room and its links, away, voices, shared panels, avatars (6e78c20, branch dee-193-together)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    direction LR
    lg0: Off, idle, or nothing held
    lg1: Live: in a room, a link whole, open, shown
    lg2: Between: calling, asking, waiting, on its way
    lg3: Ended or held back by a rule, or a wait that ran out
    lg4: Fixed T1 (6e78c20): a headset let in again while the owner still held its old link was in the room twice. TLC took 10 steps to it (PreFix, rule OnceInRoom)
    lg5: G9Together.tla: the nine rules hold in Room (719,774 states), Full (1,126,402) and Reopen (266,158), and a room always settles (Live, 14,237)
    lg6: Not run on the Frame's hardware yet: the encoder and decoder path of a shared panel (the hard reset of 2026-11-10)
    lg7: Everything a link brings is untrusted, also after its sender was let in: a link that says what it may not is closed
    lg8: Another group: arrows into it are what G9 reads or drives there
  }
  class lg0 teal
  class lg1 blue
  class lg2 yellow
  class lg3 orange
  class lg4 fixed
  class lg5 fixed
  class lg6 bugLegend
  class lg7 legendNote
  class lg8 xgroup
  state "Together on this Frame (together/run.sh, frametop-together.service, the four frametop-room-* units PartOf it)" as un {
    u0: Not installed: the installer's optional part
    [*] --> u0
    u1: Installed, off: no unit runs, nothing listens
    u2: On: ft-together waits for Tailscale, looks every 3 s
    u3: On: takes calls on the tailnet address (port 47193), the room programs beside it
  }
  state "The session on one Frame (session.h Mode, G9Together.tla)" as se {
    m0: Idle: no room
    [*] --> m0
    m1: Hosting: its room is the room
    m2: Calling a room's owner with a code
    m3: Joined: holds the room as its owner last told it
  }
  state "A link at the owner's end (session.cpp Link::State)" as lo {
    o0: Stranger: 10 s to say Hello, 8 at once
    [*] --> o0
    o1: Asking: the code was good, a card on the Together page, 120 s
    o2: Member: a person of the room
    o3: Refused or closed: told why, the link ends
  }
  state "A guest's links (session.cpp OnHello, Knocked, Mesh, OnRoom)" as lg {
    c0: Called the owner: Hello sent, 10 s
    [*] --> c0
    c1: The owner's Hello came: waits for the answer, 130 s
    c2: Member: the link to the room's owner
    p0: Called another guest: the lower address calls, 10 s
    p1: Member: a link to another guest, for poses, voice, panels, avatars
    w0: Stranger: another guest calls
    w1: Waiting: their Hello came, the room doesn't list them yet, 10 s
    p2: Closed: the room no longer lists them there, or the wait ran out. Called again 3 s on
  }
  state "Away (ft-roomaway teller.py, session SetAway)" as aw {
    a0: Here: worn, not paused
    [*] --> a0
    a1: In a game: Frametop paused. The voice stays, shared screens stand still
    a2: Headset off: the microphone closed, nothing played
  }
  state "Your voice and mouth (ft-roomvoice sender.cpp, mouthsay.h, local/mouth.h)" as vo {
    v0: Microphone closed: no room, muted, or the headset off
    [*] --> v0
    v1: Open: Opus each 20 ms to every member link, the mouth's five shapes to ft-together
    v2: Mouth in each pose sent, held 0.5 s after it was last told
    v3: Failed to open: tried again
  }
  state "A screen of yours in the room (ft-roompanels keeper.py, screens/share.c, ft-sharepanel)" as sh {
    x0: Not shared
    [*] --> x0
    x1: In the room, nobody watches: no pictures asked for, the encoder closed
    x2: Watched: encoded once for everyone, a stream a picture
    x3: A viewer waits for a keyframe: asked of the encoder, twice a second at most
  }
  state "Someone's panel here (keeper.py _others, remote.c peer, ft-peerpanel, flow/video.h)" as pe {
    y0: In the room, no screen for it here yet
    [*] --> y0
    y1: A remote screen (116 down), ft-peerpanel waits for a keyframe
    y2: In step: pictures in order, decoded, shown where the room has it
    y3: Lost its place: held pictures, nothing passed for 0.3 s
  }
  state "The avatar someone has on (flow/looks.h, local/wardrobe.h, avatar/room/sentbody.h)" as lk {
    k0: None listed: the abstract figure
    [*] --> k0
    k1: Listed: the room has its file's size and SHA-256, no file here
    k2: Asked for on the link to its wearer: awaited, to that size
    k3: Kept: the size and the hash are the room's (runtime folder, 4 at most, never parsed here)
    k4: Drawn: the strict reader took it, a body, marked as one to pass on
    k5: Refused, said once: the abstract figure stays
  }
  state "Your avatar for the others (wardrobe.cpp Wear, roomavatar.py, ft-model-import --allow-share)" as wr {
    z0: None on (AVATAR_MODEL empty): the others see the abstract figure
    [*] --> z0
    z1: On, not marked: it stays on this headset, the Together page asks
    z2: On and marked: the room lists it (an owner's at once, a guest's told every 2 s until it does)
    z3: Its file goes to who asked: 3 at once, then one in 30 s a link
  }
  state "Other groups" as og {
    g1: G1 Lifecycle and presence
    g2: G2 Desktop and panels
    g5: G5 Hands
    g6: G6 Remote displays
  }
  un --> se: ft-together holds the session
  se --> lo: an owner's links
  se --> lg: a guest's links
  aw --> vo: away off closes the microphone
  se --> sh: only in a room
  se --> lk: the room lists what each has on
  u0 --> u1: the installer's Together part, or together/run.sh install
  u1 --> u2: the Settings switch, or run.sh on: enable --now
  u2 --> u3: tailscaled says who this Frame is (Start, net/tailnet.cpp)
  u3 --> u1: the switch off: SIGTERM leaves the room first, the four units stop with it
  u3 --> u2: it ends otherwise: Restart=on-failure, 3 s
  m0 --> m1: open (Open): you stand on the owner's spot
  m0 --> m2: join HOST PORT CODE (Join)
  m2 --> m3: Welcome: your place and the room
  m2 --> m0: Refuse, no answer in time, the link down, or leave
  m3 --> m0: leave, the owner's Leave, the link to the owner lost, or taken out of the room
  m1 --> m0: leave: Leave to every member, the room ends for everyone
  m1 --> o0: someone calls
  o0 --> o1: Hello with a code that works once, for ten minutes (Asked, invites.h)
  o0 --> o3: no room open, the room full, a bad code, another version, or 10 s
  o1 --> o2: accept (Answer): a place, Room to the others, Welcome to them
  o1 --> o3: decline, or 120 s with no answer
  o2 --> o3: their Leave, the link down, or a word they may not say: Remove, Room to the others
  o2 --> o3: (fixed T1 6e78c20) the same headset is let in again: its old link closed and its old place out first
  m2 --> c0: Call
  c0 --> c1: the owner's Hello: the code was good
  c1 --> c2: Welcome
  c2 --> p0: Mesh: each guest the room lists with a higher address and no link yet
  p0 --> p1: their Hello, of this room
  p0 --> p2: Refuse, another room, or 10 s
  w0 --> w1: Hello of this room (OnHello)
  w0 --> p2: not in a room, or another room: Refuse
  w1 --> p1: Knocked: the room lists someone at that address who has no link yet
  w1 --> p2: 10 s
  p1 --> p2: Room no longer lists them there (OnRoom), their Leave, or the link down
  p2 --> p0: Tick: Mesh again, 3 s after the last call
  c2 --> m0: Room without your place, Leave, or the link down: End
  a0 --> a1: the relay says paused (pause ?), asked each second in a room
  a1 --> a0: not paused
  a0 --> a2: the pointer helper says not worn (gaze ? headset)
  a1 --> a2: not worn: the headset off wins over a game
  a2 --> a0: worn again
  a0 --> g1: G1: the worn answer and the pause are read there
  v0 --> v1: in a room, unmuted, not away off
  v1 --> v0: mute, the room left, or away off: the mouth is told shut once
  v0 --> v3: the microphone can't be opened
  v3 --> v0: the next try
  v1 --> v2: 0x83 and five weights as they change
  v2 --> v1: told again within 0.5 s
  v2 --> v0: not told for 0.5 s: the poses carry a shut mouth
  v2 --> g5: G5: the hands in the same pose come from hand tracking
  x0 --> x1: share N: Share to the room (a guest's goes through the owner), ft-screens share N start
  x1 --> x2: a Watch from a member who has it in view
  x2 --> x3: someone begins, lost their place, or a picture to them was given up
  x3 --> x2: the keyframe puts everyone in step
  x2 --> x1: nobody watches any more
  x1 --> x0: unshare N, the room left, or ft-roompanels ends
  x2 --> x0: unshare N, the room left, or ft-roompanels ends
  x2 --> g2: G2: ft-screens hands the screen's buffers over, and draws it while watched
  y0 --> y1: keeper: remote N peer ID
  y1 --> y2: a keyframe from the owner's link
  y2 --> y3: pictures overtook one another and the gap didn't fill
  y3 --> y1: Watch says the decoder needs a keyframe
  y2 --> y0: the panel left the room or changed size, or the room was left
  y1 --> g6: G6: a peer's panel is a remote screen, numbered down from 116
  k0 --> k1: Room: their Look
  k1 --> k2: Want (looks.cpp), 6 Looks and Wants at once and 1 a second a link
  k2 --> k3: the stream's bytes are that size and hash, from the one who has it on
  k2 --> k1: it didn't come: asked again after 30 s and its time at 64 KB a second
  k3 --> k4: ft-avatars --room: looks each second, sentbody reads the file
  k3 --> k5: not a whole avatar, no body, or not marked
  k4 --> k0: they take it off, leave, or the room ends: the file goes
  k5 --> k0: they take it off, leave, or the room ends
  z0 --> z1: an avatar from a glTF or FBX, or a VRM whose licence forbids passing it on
  z0 --> z2: a VRM whose licence allows it, or a model imported with --may-share
  z1 --> z2: Let them have it, and yes: ft-model-import --allow-share (never for a VRM that forbids it)
  z2 --> z3: a Want for exactly that file from someone in the room
  z3 --> z2: sent
  z2 --> z0: another avatar or none on (wear, every 2 s from ft-avatars --room)
